schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-js-04-edge-integration-state-accessibility
type: interactive
quality: high
solution: kino-js
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: edge-integration-state-accessibility
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.JS or Kino.JS.Live. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize validation, state safety, accessibility, and fallback behavior.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.JS edge/integration widget that accepts user-provided labels or records as data, validates them in Elixir before sending to the browser, renders them safely with textContent, and optionally loads one external JavaScript or CSS asset through ctx.importJS or ctx.importCSS with a visible fallback if loading fails. If two-way state is needed, use Kino.JS.Live with handle_connect and validated handle_event payloads.

    Requirements: use current module asset syntax; document Livebook compatibility, JSON serialization limits, and browser support; include scoped CSS, accessible roles and labels, keyboard interaction, reduced-motion support, and safe fallback UI; include safe execution checks for untrusted HTML, eval, external asset failure, event spoofing, non-serializable terms, credentials, shell calls, and global namespace or style leaks.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-js-edge-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino and defines a current Kino.JS or Kino.JS.Live module with asset \"main.js\"."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino runtime, JSON serialization limits, and optional external asset behavior."
  - "Reactive state: browser events and optional Live state are validated, bounded, and synchronized for late clients."
  - "Data shape: input labels or records are sanitized into JSON-serializable maps/lists with documented fallback defaults."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: ARIA roles, labels, keyboard support, reduced-motion handling, scoped CSS, and fallback UI are present."
  - "Safe execution: no eval, unsanitized innerHTML, non-serializable terms, credentials, shell calls, unchecked external asset assumptions, or style leaks."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and uses current Kino.JS asset APIs."
    - "External asset loading, if present, is awaited and guarded with fallback behavior."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements edge validation, safe rendering, optional asset integration, and state synchronization."
    - "Uses current Kino.JS or Kino.JS.Live APIs and documents serialization and browser boundaries."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Fallback and normal states are visibly distinct and accessible."
    - "Controls and dynamic regions support keyboard and screen-reader use."
    - "Scoped styling prevents interference with other Livebook cells."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles malformed input, asset load failure, event spoofing, late clients, and missing data."
    - "Keeps payloads bounded and serializable."
    - "Avoids unsafe HTML, global side effects, and unbounded browser work."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.JS-centered and treats browser integration as an explicitly validated boundary."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-js
- edge-integration-state-accessibility
